Ques:-

A colleague has started a new ML project at /root/code/fraud-detection/, but the layout does not match the xFusionCorp Industries standard. Bring the project in line with the team's conventions.

1. Inspect the existing project at /root/code/fraud-detection/.

2. The final layout must match the tree below exactly:

fraud-detection/
├── data/
│   ├── raw/
│   └── processed/
├── models/
├── notebooks/
├── src/
│   ├── data/
│   ├── features/
│   ├── models/
│   └── utils/
├── tests/
├── configs/
├── requirements.txt
└── README.md

3. Every subdirectory under src/ must contain an __init__.py file so that Python recognises it as a package.

4. requirements.txt must list the following dependencies, one per line: scikit-learn, pandas, numpy, and mlflow. The canonical PyPI name for the scikit-learn package is scikit-learn.

5. README.md must begin with the heading # fraud-detection.

6. Review the existing project and correct everything that does not match the requirements above.




Soln:-

Step 1:- Create missing top-level directories

mkdir -p /root/code/fraud-detection/tests/
mkdir -p /root/code/fraud-detection/configs/
mkdir -p /root/code/fraud-detection/data/raw
mkdir -p /root/code/fraud-detection/data/processed



Step 2:- Fix names inside src (rename feature → features, util → utils)

mv /root/code/fraud-detection/src/feature /root/code/fraud-detection/src/features
mv /root/code/fraud-detection/src/util /root/code/fraud-detection/src/utils



Step 3:- Ensuring "__init__.py" exists in each src subdirectory

touch /root/code/fraud-detection/src/data/__init__.py
touch /root/code/fraud-detection/src/features/__init__.py
touch /root/code/fraud-detection/src/models/__init__.py
touch /root/code/fraud-detection/src/utils/__init__.py



Step 4:- Correct the requirements.txt file (Ensured requirements.txt contains exactly:)

scikit-learn
pandas
numpy
mlflow



Step 5:- Updated README.md so it begins with

# fraud-detection
